cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Project Lambda: is market conductance a forecastable state variable?
message: If you use this work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Project Lambda contributors
abstract: >-
  A free-data falsification study of the market impact operator. Tests whether
  conductance - the operator converting shocks into price movement - is a
  forecastable state variable, and whether it is explained by the discretion
  distribution of the holder base. Finds the former holds universally across ten
  asset classes and the latter is not supported, including on scheduled FOMC
  decisions where the predicted coefficient is excluded at 5.4 standard errors.
keywords:
  - market microstructure
  - price impact
  - Kyle lambda
  - Amihud illiquidity
  - gold
  - commitments of traders
  - inelastic markets
  - falsification
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-06
